 #uuid "206ffe09-0bf2-52fa-9f10-25e3482f34a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263853/field-1/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-263853/field-1/9e0ecd3ac52ff99368669f5f34617bf0346b508d0e5368e317a2e814e87142d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263853" :question/id #uuid "30fb49ab-a6e3-5a66-bbff-a23fc2c189c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-263853" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.2,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.85,$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cap B).$\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cap B)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.85 & =0.5+P(B)-0.2 \\\\ P(B) & =0.85-0.5+0.2 \\\\ P(B) & =0.55\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cap B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/43267ee39b162c12235739ea84e9be539015ea28627caf14828b5fb5cc9fcd7b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cap B)=0.35.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263853/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d5731e2-34fa-5e27-84be-324dc958b509"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-179490/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "935baa6f-d65d-5250-8672-f7db0acde8e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179490/selection/09f9568b9032a258744b73b08553a45679ce3baf10e1847349ddb9cf78a3d261" :answer/id #uuid "69131d78-28bb-52b3-992c-f0d804aecdc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179490/selection/8792e560466dad9193d7afed2fdbb634744