ally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup B)=0.1+0.2+0.4=0.7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-178681/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-178681"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-264077"] :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\frac{1}{4},$ $P(B)=\\frac{1}{6},$ and $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{12},$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup B).$ Do not round your answer.\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cup B)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{12}+\\frac{2}{12}-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/0c8d9572472da406cf84f5657d0ea47d0d1ba76592c98d4e6f442ecb9ef03dec.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup B)=\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-264413/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "a347f503-e59c-596b-a7c3-13ce21105897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264413/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "8a647118-d024-5177-a8ec-298eb2d02e89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264413/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e27fdb-5393-5bc6-b382-45d17479f361" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264413/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-264413/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-264413/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264413" :question/id #uuid "0c42571e-fe28-594c-ae53-f8b3f913ae73" :question/math-academy-id "q-264413" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{2}{5},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{3},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{5}{6},$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}).$ Do not round your answer.\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{5}{6} & =P(A)+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{30}+\\frac{10}{30}-\\frac{12}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/4b5f335b449e5f07de1d9ac1590245e71f6825b2dc13fe4ba046985aac95465a.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}) & =\\frac{13}{30}+\\frac{1}{15}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{30}+\\frac{2}{30}+\\frac{5}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264413/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264409/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "942b06da-a9f1-55b1-9c64-62c9c20ea447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264409/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de503ca4-d638-54fa-a418-7fa4026034fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264409/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer-field/choices ["q-264409/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264409" :question/id #uuid "c97475b3-cbd6-51db-9270-19307459760f" :question/math-academy-id "q-264409" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=0.6,$ $P(B)=0.5,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.6+0.5-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.6+0.5-0.8 \\\\  & =0.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/7ed0c9bf5b752eeffcd869d1b511d9ff65ca7cbbc6f5d85a38012b5ba57460d0.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′})=0.3+0.2+0.2=0.7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264409/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264419/field-1/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "6ee4b295-d4d7-5db5-80e6-a155eebdf795" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264419/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "33c077e8-c1f3-5bda-871e-018b31575129" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264419/field-1/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer-field/choices ["q-264419/field-1/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264419" :question/id #uuid "0dc08ae8-67ca-5c40-90cc-3c486588dfde" :question/math-academy-id "q-264419" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=0.6,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.25,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.95,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$\n\n$P({B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.95 & =0.6+P(B)-0.25 \\\\ P(B) & =0.95+0.25-0.6 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.6 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264419/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264419"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264415/field-1/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "d1c040bc-c7a3-50b1-b43d-db040a876690" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264415/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f" :answer/id #uuid "b16c18a4-c591-5800-8b60-5fbe6680ead6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264415/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e433324a-9117-5f51-b34d-b07e9aab9098" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264415/field-1/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-264415/field-1/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-264415/field-1/441f9a41e4c1d7c29719a73a7d795c394ee1337b1a990ebfb59a7b69a254418f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264415" :question/id #uuid "de355132-c934-56e3-9f81-8d3f91957eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-264415" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=0.35,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.15,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$\n\n$P({B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =0.35+P(B)-0.15 \\\\ P(B) & =0.9+0.15-0.35 \\\\  & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264415/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "667c86f2-b962-5193-9d39-077487e14b00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "140dfabc-7daf-5653-bcf3-f21ca835a86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" :answer/id #uuid "ec216eb9-efcf-5730-9954-2ddd73274bba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528/selection/22bbee0d8e9610e940e635938755e10bd27ffea1adddb9664ad643e6998d9bdf" :answer/id #uuid "96ff8959-b005-5b48-b41b-11ea13bcd772" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer/id #uuid "29bfca27-96cf-5eb9-90a4-7e30166a3407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cead592a-00a2-5162-8515-d80c33cd881b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-179528/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer-field/choices ["q-179528/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-179528/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" "q-179528/selection/47e062f84c7679179a100f841000c1550fcbc886f881ad4b3253348673d23026" "q-179528/selection/22bbee0d8e9610e940e635938755e10bd27ffea1adddb9664ad643e6998d9bdf" "q-179528/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-179528" :question/id #uuid "ac701741-50dd-53b0-a6f5-96fdac1ca3b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-179528" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=0.7,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.3,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P({A}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =P(A)+0.7-0.3 \\\\ P(A) & =0.9+0.3-0.7 \\\\ P(A) & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.5 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-179528/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-179528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264425/field-1/23345b14c05e80f14e1d1ace7f3cc0733762398f823dd8d75f85be8a9c643ed4" :answer/id #uuid "841313af-bf32-53b9-946a-def406998832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{63}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264425/field-1/fdfdcf75cf3409641afccc080eb0e07448b4313487bc25c6a5c6dbd30decdf36" :answer/id #uuid "a3187a80-7e7e-57c8-90e7-7c6b22d5ec69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{44}{63}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264425/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "63d6fb2c-f075-5a52-8679-30a886388c3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264425/field-1/23345b14c05e80f14e1d1ace7f3cc0733762398f823dd8d75f85be8a9c643ed4" :answer-field/choices ["q-264425/field-1/23345b14c05e80f14e1d1ace7f3cc0733762398f823dd8d75f85be8a9c643ed4" "q-264425/field-1/fdfdcf75cf3409641afccc080eb0e07448b4313487bc25c6a5c6dbd30decdf36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264425" :question/id #uuid "35262bb8-e0ee-5d22-a309-9c8333f109bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-264425" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\frac{1}{3},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{7},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{8}{9},$ find $P({B}^{′}).$ Do not round your answer.\n\n$P({B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{8}{9} & =\\frac{1}{3}+P(B)-\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{8}{9}+\\frac{1}{7}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{44}{63}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{44}{63} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{63}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264425/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "1bdd93ae-ac8a-589f-ba4b-edad509eb65a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529/selection/0d247918008ed78cc89a6965d62d9f4a8fe02d275ec22142df80e82512aa1ea1" :answer/id #uuid "255224e6-4df9-520e-8b5f-d278dcf56e23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529/selection/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05" :answer/id #uuid "6442d7c0-65dc-5ffe-952a-1e463ae32f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "f97da505-8504-5d77-96a8-531410768d07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer/id #uuid "668c6302-609b-5f22-9317-349f1d79253c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe3cee9-ac6e-5a14-b6bb-996390fb54a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-179529/selection/0d247918008ed78cc89a6965d62d9f4a8fe02d275ec22142df80e82512aa1ea1" :answer-field/choices ["q-179529/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-179529/selection/0d247918008ed78cc89a6965d62d9f4a8fe02d275ec22142df80e82512aa1ea1" "q-179529/selection/1512fbc4ba9ac54935748bd30a3df0f8adcca19968544e9199178dd45a802f05" "q-179529/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-179529/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-179529" :question/id #uuid "7fd4115d-263b-5a50-bff1-4f2f0d0e78fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-179529" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{1}{2},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{4},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{2}{3},$ find $P({A}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =P(A)+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-179529/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-179529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13034"] :question/problem "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/ca3ae8f8df5bb20c40261cb25dbfdcf31a71717c01b6ef820c5c5ded2aedbbfc.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6071a2687c038fe8b7e95abe89c07b93aebe21424fadde72eb5ac52e64771895.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6a2c9b8bfdd3b9c0f642c1a96f8914926a2ef7c2f0aacdc536cee42760a63448.png), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/7ca88e3705a778b7a8329a2a7ae3248a377a79aa2a88bee51e7360dd36536e82.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9b7b7cbb7f22bed24e5dafdfdbb4e29cc434eaeeb361ac601673654299dfedd0.png) using the addition law\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8ac1b158770eacf57e651320b9aff02492fa6693383cd5c07c43fbcf439a3141.png)\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8951b2f0456d6317f684dba75a4eb098bfeeb6fa77ec83947d4e2f09baadaece.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/bac5655a5b79a32e8155e26be50275409a6bbf41b939cfb823e5e53fccef6663.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/dc3c94937b19dc1efda8aa5356c0985fc6833d85cdfa1437a5fc60c88e018de9.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12933"] :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12,$ $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16,$ and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23,$ find $P(A'\\cup B').$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}+P(B)-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9856c9b0fdf3bf4b8f84417f6e625d823590f57dac4dcc8185994aef3f8c5e50.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13035"] :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=0.6,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P(A').$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =P(A)+0.6-0.4 \\\\ P(A) & =0.9+0.4-0.6 \\\\ P(A) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
